This poem entitled "Keep Going" was written by Edgar Albert Guest
for the March 4, 1921 issue of the _Detroit Free Press_.

There exists a tape recording of my great-grandfather reciting this poem,
among certain others in this book.
I have kept some of his variations to the wording:
- #quote[Many a fool has turned about]
  instead of #quote[Many a failure turns about]
- #quote[when the night came down]
  instead of #quote[when the night slipped down]
